  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "owners",
      "chapter": "One file, several owners",
      "text": "A coding agent opens a NetworkX file. Earlier commits survive in memory if any participating file still retains them. The two columns show which reads change.",
      "start_frame": 0,
      "frames": 296,
      "steady_frames": 296,
      "render_sha256": "cc1988b13e69565872362b768c09381a06416d6085cd8a9156bbd4e4efa4ca84"
    },
    {
      "id": "receipts",
      "chapter": "Inspect a previous change",
      "text": "Open a source event to see which file retained it. In this example the test for the directed generator moves into the eight recommendations.",
      "start_frame": 296,
      "frames": 230,
      "steady_frames": 227,
      "render_sha256": "65d0e2b74010ff23dba7d09771f4e649e91e39eacba8550c395e083a39788b14"
    },
    {
      "id": "cold",
      "chapter": "Restart without a snapshot",
      "text": "The archive still returns the exact eight files after the process restarts. Start with an empty cache and inspect the traffic required for the next 196 queries.",
      "start_frame": 526,
      "frames": 300,
      "steady_frames": 297,
      "render_sha256": "3451b83d2d3d9ce0881e243ddf30925d7442e0b29126720c7e956d81372f5934"
    },
    {
      "id": "recent",
      "chapter": "Checkpoint the most recent events",
      "text": "Give each repository one kibibyte for a snapshot. Choosing the most recent events produces about the same total traffic as the cold start.",
      "start_frame": 826,
      "frames": 246,
      "steady_frames": 243,
      "render_sha256": "a24b9671369c4ff74b47048f1fcd779be8572f37f33607b6e31a55d4441c6457"
    },
    {
      "id": "demand",
      "chapter": "Choose events from past file activity",
      "text": "Keep the budget fixed and select events using past file activity. Total transfer falls to about eighty-three thousand bytes, including snapshot writes and reads.",
      "start_frame": 1072,
      "frames": 287,
      "steady_frames": 284,
      "render_sha256": "060f7bce7607e3b6f6429254a20718053824ce4e44df84cc9230d149e13adf0f"
    },
    {
      "id": "negative",
      "chapter": "Inspect a case with higher cost",
      "text": "On shorter histories the four-kibibyte padded snapshot costs more than a cold start. The price of writing and loading it exceeds the savings from future reads.",
      "start_frame": 1359,
      "frames": 267,
      "steady_frames": 264,
      "render_sha256": "7340f4aa173c8c08fea0e0c350124c2a2c1feff0859fc32af667da742651490b"
    },
    {
      "id": "full",
      "chapter": "Remove the fixed-size padding",
      "text": "On the same panel the whole snapshot is small. Choosing the full snapshot stores the actual contents and reduces total traffic to about twelve thousand bytes.",
      "start_frame": 1626,
      "frames": 269,
      "steady_frames": 266,
      "render_sha256": "5a78f9046562b7c1bafc04e6e8a4516657baecd40ae9809fd71a7665ba3e813b"
    },
    {
      "id": "text",
      "chapter": "Reuse a previous editor view",
      "text": "Open the recorded agent reads. Compare storing each line separately with sharing its contents. The local cache must still match the path and line number.",
      "start_frame": 1895,
      "frames": 277,
      "steady_frames": 274,
      "render_sha256": "4ae441ca410dcb6583eff5741517716cf772328fdf7fe464c67708dc0ccc6299"
    },
    {
      "id": "gold",
      "chapter": "Check ranking quality separately",
      "text": "In this real Dask query the two files are known. Reveal the held-out paths. A rule using joint evidence finds two, while a simpler control finds all three.",
